IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-logic`

-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III, sections 22B to 22F -- layer 1: a court may order a business in the regulated sector to hand over
-- information; the four conditions; what the order must say; what happens on non-compliance; privilege; statements; appeals.
-- "A business in the regulated sector" turns on Schedule 3A, "the criminal intelligence function" on the Crime and Courts Act 2013,
-- the sum in s 22B(8) on regulations under s 22B(10): none of these is among the sources, so each is a fact the caller states
-- (the £5,000 itself is in the text).  Sections 22B(10) and (11), 22E(5) and 22F(1) to (6) and (9) are machinery (rule- and
-- regulation-making and code-making powers): inert, reason 2.

§ `Part III Terrorist Property -- Information orders`

§§ `s 22B Information orders`

-- src:441 | (4) Condition 1 for the making of an information order is met if—
-- src:442 | (a) the information required to be given under the order would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under section 21A,
-- src:443 | (b) the respondent is the person who made the disclosure or is otherwise carrying on a business in the regulated sector,
-- src:444 | (c) the information would assist in—
-- src:445 | (i) investigating whether a person is involved in the commission of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 or in determining whether an investigation of that kind should be started, or
-- src:446 | (ii) identifying terrorist property or its movement or use, and
-- src:447 | (d) it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided.
@ref s 22B(4) (src:441-447)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Info order condition 1 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(4) condition 1 is met` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the information required would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under s 21A`
           AND (`the facts`'s `the respondent is the person who made the disclosure` OR `the facts`'s `the respondent is otherwise carrying on a business in the regulated sector`)
           AND (`the facts`'s `the information would assist in investigating whether a person is involved in the commission of an offence under any of sections 15 to 18 or in determining whether an investigation of that kind should be started`
                OR `the facts`'s `the information would assist in identifying terrorist property or its movement or use`)
           AND `the facts`'s `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 1 for the making of an information order is met if—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:448 | (5) Condition 2 for the making of an information order is met if—
-- src:449 | (a) the information required to be given under the order would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under a corresponding disclosure requirement,
-- src:450 | (b) an external request has been made to the National Crime Agency for the provision of information in connection with that disclosure,
-- src:451 | (c) the respondent is carrying on a business in the regulated sector,
-- src:452 | (d) the information is likely to be of substantial value to the authority that made the external request in determining any matter in connection with the disclosure, and
-- src:453 | (e) it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided.
@ref s 22B(5) (src:448-453)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Info order condition 2 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(5) condition 2 is met` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the information required would relate to a matter arising from a disclosure made under a corresponding disclosure requirement`
           AND `the facts`'s `an external request has been made to the National Crime Agency for the provision of information in connection with that disclosure`
           AND `the facts`'s `the respondent is carrying on a business in the regulated sector`
           AND `the facts`'s `the information is likely to be of substantial value to the authority that made the external request in determining any matter in connection with the disclosure`
           AND `the facts`'s `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 2 for the making of an information order is met if—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:454 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5), “external request” means a request made by an authority of a foreign country which has responsibility in that country for carrying out investigations into whether a corresponding terrorist financing offence has been committed.
@ref s 22B(6) (src:454)
GIVEN `the request is made by an authority of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has responsibility in that country for carrying out investigations into whether a corresponding terrorist financing offence has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(6) the request is an external request` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the request is made by an authority of a foreign country`
           AND `the authority has responsibility in that country for carrying out investigations into whether a corresponding terrorist financing offence has been committed`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“external request” means a request made by an authority of a foreign country which has responsibility in that country for carrying out investigations"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:455 | (6A) Condition 3 for the making of an information order is met if—
-- src:456 | (a) the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct—
-- src:457 | (i) operational analysis of information that is relevant to terrorist financing or suspected terrorist financing, or
-- src:458 | (ii) strategic analysis identifying trends or patterns in the conduct of terrorist financing, or systemic deficiencies or vulnerabilities which have been, are being or are likely to be, exploited for the purposes of terrorist financing,
-- src:459 | for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency so far as it relates to terrorist financing,
-- src:460 | (b) the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector,
-- src:461 | (c) where the application for the order is made to a magistrates’ court, the person making the application has had regard to the code of practice under section 22F,
-- src:462 | (d) where the application for the order is made to the sheriff—
-- src:463 | (i) the application is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer, and
-- src:464 | (ii) the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under section 22F, and
-- src:465 | (e) it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided.
@ref s 22B(6A) (src:455-465)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Info order condition 3 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(6A) condition 3 is met` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the facts`'s `the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct operational analysis of information that is relevant to terrorist financing or suspected terrorist financing`
            OR `the facts`'s `the information would assist an authorised NCA officer to conduct strategic analysis identifying trends or patterns in the conduct of terrorist financing, or systemic deficiencies or vulnerabilities`)
           AND `the facts`'s `that analysis is for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency so far as it relates to terrorist financing`
           AND `the facts`'s `the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector`
           AND ((NOT `the facts`'s `the application is made to a magistrates court`) OR `the facts`'s `the person making the application has had regard to the code of practice under s 22F`)
           AND ((NOT `the facts`'s `the application is made to the sheriff`)
                OR (`the facts`'s `the application is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer`
                    AND `the facts`'s `the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under s 22F`))
           AND `the facts`'s `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 3 for the making of an information order is met if—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:466 | (6B) Condition 4 for the making of an information order is met if—
-- src:467 | (a) a request has been made by a foreign FIU to the National Crime Agency for the provision of the information required to be given under the order,
-- src:468 | (b) an authorised NCA officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the request was made only for the purpose of assisting the foreign FIU to conduct one or both of the following—
-- src:469 | (i) operational analysis of information that is relevant to terrorist financing or suspected terrorist financing, or
-- src:470 | (ii) strategic analysis identifying trends or patterns in the conduct of terrorist financing, or systematic deficiencies or vulnerabilities which have been, are being or are likely to be, exploited for the purposes of terrorist financing,
-- src:471 | and that the information is likely to be of substantial value to the foreign FIU in carrying out such analysis,
-- src:472 | (c) the provision of the information by the National Crime Agency to the foreign FIU would be for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function of the National Crime Agency, so far as it relates to terrorist financing,
-- src:473 | (d) the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector,
-- src:474 | (e) where the application for the order is made to a magistrates’ court, the person making the application has had regard to the code of practice under section 22F,
-- src:475 | (f) where the application for the order is made to the sheriff—
-- src:476 | (i) the application is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer, and
-- src:477 | (ii) the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under section 22F, and
-- src:478 | (g) it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided.
@ref s 22B(6B) (src:466-478)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Info order condition 4 facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(6B) condition 4 is met` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `a request has been made by a foreign FIU to the National Crime Agency for the provision of the information required to be given under the order`
           AND `the facts`'s `an authorised NCA officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the request was made only for the purpose of assisting the foreign FIU to conduct operational or strategic analysis`
           AND `the facts`'s `an authorised NCA officer has reasonable grounds to believe that the information is likely to be of substantial value to the foreign FIU in carrying out such analysis`
           AND `the facts`'s `the provision of the information by the National Crime Agency to the foreign FIU would be for the purposes of the criminal intelligence function so far as it relates to terrorist financing`
           AND `the facts`'s `the respondent is a person carrying on a business in the regulated sector`
           AND ((NOT `the facts`'s `the application is made to a magistrates court`) OR `the facts`'s `the person making the application has had regard to the code of practice under s 22F`)
           AND ((NOT `the facts`'s `the application is made to the sheriff`)
                OR (`the facts`'s `the application is made by a procurator fiscal at the request of the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer`
                    AND `the facts`'s `the person making that request has had regard to the code of practice under s 22F`))
           AND `the facts`'s `it is reasonable in all the circumstances for the information to be provided`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition 4 for the making of an information order is met if—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:429 | (1) A magistrates’ court or (in Scotland) the sheriff may, on an application made by a law enforcement officer, make an information order if satisfied that either condition 1 or condition 2 is met.
@ref s 22B(1) (src:429)
GIVEN `the application is made by a law enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `condition 2` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(1) the court may make an information order` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is made by a law enforcement officer` AND (conditions EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, on an application made by a law enforcement officer, make an information order if satisfied that either condition 1 or condition 2 is met" (a power given "if" a condition is met: when the applicant is not a law enforcement officer, or neither condition is met, the "if" fails; ruling of 2026-11-05)
        IF (NOT `the application is made by a law enforcement officer`) OR (conditions EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        conditions MEANS `the disjunction` `condition 1` `or else` `condition 2`

-- src:430 | (1A) A magistrates’ court or (in Scotland) the sheriff may, on an application made—
-- src:431 | (a) in the case of a magistrates’ court, by the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer, and
-- src:432 | (b) in the case of the sheriff, by a procurator fiscal,
-- src:433 | make an information order if satisfied that either condition 3 or condition 4 is met.
@ref s 22B(1A) (src:430-433)
GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court that decided`
      `the application is made by the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by a procurator fiscal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition 3` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `condition 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(1A) the court may make an information order` IS
    BRANCH
        IF applicant AND (conditions EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, on an application made— (a) in the case of a magistrates' court, by the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer, and (b) in the case of the sheriff, by a procurator fiscal, make an information order if satisfied that either condition 3 or condition 4 is met" (a power given "if" a condition is met: when the applicant is not the person the paragraph names, or neither condition is met, the "if" fails; ruling of 2026-11-05)
        IF (NOT applicant) OR (conditions EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        applicant MEANS
            CONSIDER `the court`
            WHEN `a magistrates court in England and Wales` THEN `the application is made by the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer`
            WHEN `a magistrates court in Northern Ireland` THEN `the application is made by the Director General of the National Crime Agency or an authorised NCA officer`
            WHEN `the sheriff` THEN `the application is made by a procurator fiscal`
        conditions MEANS `the disjunction` `condition 3` `or else` `condition 4`

-- src:434 | (2) The application must—
-- src:435 | (a) specify or describe the information sought under the order, and
-- src:436 | (b) specify the person from whom the information is sought (“the respondent”).
@ref s 22B(2) (src:434-436)
GIVEN `the application specifies or describes the information sought under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application specifies the person from whom the information is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(2) the application has the content the subsection requires` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application specifies or describes the information sought under the order` AND `the application specifies the person from whom the information is sought`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must— (a) specify or describe the information sought under the order, and (b) specify the person from whom the information is sought"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:437 | (3) An information order is an order requiring the respondent to provide—
-- src:438 | (a) the information specified or described in the application for the order, or
-- src:439 | (b) such other information as the court or sheriff making the order thinks appropriate,
-- src:440 | so far as the information is in the possession, or under the control, of the respondent.
@ref s 22B(3) (src:437-440)
GIVEN `the information is specified or described in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or sheriff making the order thinks it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is in the possession, or under the control, of the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(3) the order requires the respondent to provide the information` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the information is specified or described in the application` OR `the court or sheriff making the order thinks it appropriate`)
           AND `the information is in the possession, or under the control, of the respondent`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so far as the information is in the possession, or under the control, of the respondent" (information outside the respondent's possession or control is outside what the order requires, but the subsection does not say the respondent need not answer for it)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:437 | (3) An information order is an order requiring the respondent to provide—
-- src:438 | (a) the information specified or described in the application for the order, or
-- src:439 | (b) such other information as the court or sheriff making the order thinks appropriate,
-- src:440 | so far as the information is in the possession, or under the control, of the respondent.
@ref s 22B(3) (src:437-440)
GIVEN deadline IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part III` `Act under Part III`
DECIDE `s 22B(3) the respondent must provide the information the order requires` IS
    PARTY `the respondent`
    MUST `provide the information the order requires`
    WITHIN deadline
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the respondent` BECAUSE "s 22B(3) and (7): the respondent did not provide the information the information order requires, in the way and by the date the order specifies"

-- src:479 | (7) An information order must specify—
-- src:480 | (a) how the information required under the order is to be provided, and
-- src:481 | (b) the date by which it is to be provided.
@ref s 22B(7) (src:479-481)
GIVEN `the order specifies how the information required under the order is to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order specifies the date by which it is to be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(7) the order has the content the subsection requires` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order specifies how the information required under the order is to be provided` AND `the order specifies the date by which it is to be provided`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An information order must specify— (a) how the information required under the order is to be provided, and (b) the date by which it is to be provided."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:482 | (8) If a person fails to comply with an information order made by a magistrates’ court, the magistrates’ court may order the person to pay an amount not exceeding £5,000.
@ref s 22B(8) (src:482)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with an information order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was made by a magistrates court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(8) the magistrates court may order the person to pay an amount` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person fails to comply with an information order` AND `the order was made by a magistrates court`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person fails to comply with an information order made by a magistrates' court, the magistrates' court may order the person to pay" (a power given "if": no failure to comply, or an order made by the sheriff, and the "if" fails; ruling of 2026-11-05)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:482 | (8) If a person fails to comply with an information order made by a magistrates’ court, the magistrates’ court may order the person to pay an amount not exceeding £5,000.
-- src:484 | (10) In order to take account of changes in the value of money the Secretary of State may by regulations made by statutory instrument substitute another sum for the sum for the time being specified in subsection (8).
@ref s 22B(8) (src:482) (src:484)
GIVEN `the sum substituted by regulations under s 22B(10)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 22B(8) the ceiling of the amount the court may order the person to pay` IS
    CONSIDER `the sum substituted by regulations under s 22B(10)`
    WHEN JUST sum THEN sum
    -- the £5,000 stated in the subsection stands until regulations under subsection (10) substitute another sum
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 5000

-- src:483 | (9) The sum mentioned in subsection (8) is to be treated as adjudged to be paid by a conviction of the court for the purposes of the Magistrates’ Courts Act 1980 or (as the case may be) the Magistrates’ Courts (Northern Ireland) Order 1981 (S.I. 1981/1675 (N.I. 26)).
@ref s 22B(9) (src:483)
GIVEN `the sum is the sum mentioned in subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(9) the sum is treated as adjudged to be paid by a conviction of the court` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sum is the sum mentioned in subsection (8)` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The sum mentioned in subsection (8) is to be treated as adjudged to be paid by a conviction of the court" (any other sum is outside the deeming)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:486 | (12) A law enforcement officer who is a constable, a National Crime Agency officer or a counter-terrorism financial investigator may not make an application under this section in reliance on Condition 1 or 2 unless the officer is a senior law enforcement officer or is authorised to do so by a senior law enforcement officer.
@ref s 22B(12) (src:486)
GIVEN `the officer is a constable, a National Crime Agency officer or a counter-terrorism financial investigator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made in reliance on Condition 1 or 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is a senior law enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is authorised to do so by a senior law enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(12) the officer is barred from making the application` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the officer is a constable, a National Crime Agency officer or a counter-terrorism financial investigator` AND `the application is made in reliance on Condition 1 or 2`)
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A law enforcement officer who is a constable, a National Crime Agency officer or a counter-terrorism financial investigator may not make an application under this section in reliance on Condition 1 or 2" (a procurator fiscal, or an application on Condition 3 or 4, is outside the bar)
            THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the officer is a senior law enforcement officer or is authorised to do so by a senior law enforcement officer"
        IF `the officer is a senior law enforcement officer` OR `the officer is authorised to do so by a senior law enforcement officer`
            THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:486 | (12) A law enforcement officer who is a constable, a National Crime Agency officer or a counter-terrorism financial investigator may not make an application under this section in reliance on Condition 1 or 2 unless the officer is a senior law enforcement officer or is authorised to do so by a senior law enforcement officer.
@ref s 22B(12) (src:486)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part III` `Act under Part III`
DECIDE `s 22B(12) the law enforcement officer shall not make an application unless senior or authorised` IS
    PARTY `a law enforcement officer`
    SHANT `make an application for an information order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a law enforcement officer` BECAUSE "s 22B(12): a constable, National Crime Agency officer or counter-terrorism financial investigator made an application in reliance on Condition 1 or 2 without being a senior law enforcement officer or being authorised by one"

-- src:487 | (13) Schedule 3A has effect for the purposes of this section in determining what is a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 22B(13) (src:487)
GIVEN `the answer Schedule 3A gives` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(13) the business is a business in the regulated sector` IS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 3A decides what is a business in the regulated sector and is not among the sources; with no answer from it, NOTHING
    `the answer Schedule 3A gives`

-- src:489 | “authorised NCA officer” means an officer of the National Crime Agency authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for the purposes of this section;
@ref s 22B(14) authorised NCA officer (src:489)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the National Crime Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for the purposes of s 22B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(14) the person is an authorised NCA officer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an officer of the National Crime Agency` AND `the person is authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for the purposes of s 22B` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“authorised NCA officer” means an officer of the National Crime Agency authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for the purposes of this section"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:490 | “corresponding disclosure requirement” means a requirement to make a disclosure under the law of the foreign country concerned that corresponds to a requirement imposed by virtue of this Part;
@ref s 22B(14) corresponding disclosure requirement (src:490)
GIVEN `the requirement is a requirement to make a disclosure under the law of the foreign country concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it corresponds to a requirement imposed by virtue of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(14) the requirement is a corresponding disclosure requirement` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the requirement is a requirement to make a disclosure under the law of the foreign country concerned` AND `it corresponds to a requirement imposed by virtue of this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“corresponding disclosure requirement” means a requirement to make a disclosure under the law of the foreign country concerned that corresponds to a requirement imposed by virtue of this Part"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:491 | “corresponding terrorist financing offence” means an offence under the law of the foreign country concerned that would, if done in the United Kingdom, constitute an offence under any of sections 15 to 18;
@ref s 22B(14) corresponding terrorist financing offence (src:491)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence under the law of the foreign country concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would, if done in the United Kingdom, constitute an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(14) the offence is a corresponding terrorist financing offence` IS
    BRANCH
        -- fork F7: "any of sections 15 to 18" includes section 17A
        IF `the offence is an offence under the law of the foreign country concerned` AND `it would, if done in the United Kingdom, constitute an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“corresponding terrorist financing offence” means an offence under the law of the foreign country concerned that would, if done in the United Kingdom, constitute an offence under any of sections 15 to 18"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:492 | “the criminal intelligence function” has the meaning given by section 1(5) of the Crime and Courts Act 2013;
@ref s 22B(14) the criminal intelligence function (src:492)
GIVEN `the answer s 1(5) of the Crime and Courts Act 2013 gives` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(14) the function is the criminal intelligence function` IS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "“the criminal intelligence function” has the meaning given by section 1(5) of the Crime and Courts Act 2013", which is not among the sources; with no answer from it, NOTHING
    `the answer s 1(5) of the Crime and Courts Act 2013 gives`

-- src:493 | “foreign country” means a country or territory outside the United Kingdom;
@ref s 22B(14) foreign country (src:493)
GIVEN `the place is a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
