DECIDE `s 22B(14) the place is a foreign country` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the place is a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign country” means a country or territory outside the United Kingdom"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:494 | “foreign FIU” means a body in a foreign country carrying out the functions of a financial intelligence unit within the meaning of Recommendation 29 of the Financial Action Task Force (as that Recommendation has effect from time to time);
@ref s 22B(14) foreign FIU (src:494)
GIVEN `the body is in a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it carries out the functions of a financial intelligence unit within the meaning of Recommendation 29 of the Financial Action Task Force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(14) the body is a foreign FIU` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the body is in a foreign country` AND `it carries out the functions of a financial intelligence unit within the meaning of Recommendation 29 of the Financial Action Task Force` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“foreign FIU” means a body in a foreign country carrying out the functions of a financial intelligence unit"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:495 | “law enforcement officer” means—
-- src:496 | a constable,
-- src:497 | a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of this section by the Director General of that Agency,
-- src:498 | a counter-terrorism financial investigator, or
-- src:499 | a procurator fiscal;
@ref s 22B(14) law enforcement officer (src:495-499)
GIVEN `the person is a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of s 22B by the Director General of that Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a counter-terrorism financial investigator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a procurator fiscal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(14) the person is a law enforcement officer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a constable` OR `the person is a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of s 22B by the Director General of that Agency` OR `the person is a counter-terrorism financial investigator` OR `the person is a procurator fiscal` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“law enforcement officer” means— a constable, a National Crime Agency officer authorised ..., a counter-terrorism financial investigator, or a procurator fiscal"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:500 | “senior law enforcement officer” means—
-- src:501 | a police officer of at least the rank of superintendent;
-- src:502 | the Director General of the National Crime Agency;
-- src:503 | any other National Crime Agency officer authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for this purpose.
@ref s 22B(14) senior law enforcement officer (src:500-503)
GIVEN `the person is a police officer of at least the rank of superintendent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Director General of the National Crime Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is any other National Crime Agency officer authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(14) the person is a senior law enforcement officer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a police officer of at least the rank of superintendent` OR `the person is the Director General of the National Crime Agency` OR `the person is any other National Crime Agency officer authorised by the Director General (whether generally or specifically) for this purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“senior law enforcement officer” means— a police officer of at least the rank of superintendent; the Director General of the National Crime Agency; any other National Crime Agency officer authorised"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:504 | “terrorist financing” means—
-- src:505 | for the purposes of subsection (6A), an act which constitutes an offence under any of sections 15 to 18;
-- src:506 | for the purposes of subsection (6B), an act which constitutes a corresponding terrorist financing offence.
@ref s 22B(14) terrorist financing (src:504-506)
GIVEN `the condition in question` IS A `Conditions of s 22B`
      `the act constitutes an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act constitutes a corresponding terrorist financing offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22B(14) the act is terrorist financing` IS
    CONSIDER `the condition in question`
    WHEN `Condition 3` THEN
        -- fork F7: "any of sections 15 to 18" includes section 17A
        IF `the act constitutes an offence under any of sections 15 to 18` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `Condition 4` THEN
        IF `the act constitutes a corresponding terrorist financing offence` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "“terrorist financing” means— for the purposes of subsection (6A), ...; for the purposes of subsection (6B), ..." (the term is defined for conditions 3 and 4 only)
    WHEN `Condition 1` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `Condition 2` THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 22C Statements`

-- src:508 | (1) A statement made by a person in response to an information order may not be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings.
@ref s 22C(1) (src:508)
GIVEN `the statement was made by the person in response to an information order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are criminal proceedings against the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22C(1) the statement may not be used in evidence against the person` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the statement was made by the person in response to an information order` AND `the proceedings are criminal proceedings against the person`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A statement made by a person in response to an information order may not be used in evidence against the person in criminal proceedings." (a statement made otherwise, or used in other proceedings, is outside the bar)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:509 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply—
-- src:510 | (a) in the case of proceedings under this Part,
-- src:511 | (b) on a prosecution for perjury, or
-- src:512 | (c) on a prosecution for some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 22C(2) (src:509-512)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are a prosecution for perjury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are a prosecution for some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22C(2) subsection (1) does not apply` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are proceedings under this Part` OR `the proceedings are a prosecution for perjury` OR `the proceedings are a prosecution for some other offence where, in giving evidence, the person makes a statement inconsistent with the statement mentioned in subsection (1)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply— (a) in the case of proceedings under this Part, (b) on a prosecution for perjury, or (c) ..." (in any other case the subsection says nothing)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:513 | (3) A statement may not be used by virtue of subsection (2)(c) unless—
-- src:514 | (a) evidence relating to it is adduced, or
-- src:515 | (b) a question relating to it is asked,
-- src:516 | by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution.
@ref s 22C(3) (src:513-516)
GIVEN `use of the statement is sought by virtue of subsection (2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `evidence relating to it is adduced by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question relating to it is asked by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22C(3) the statement may not be used by virtue of subsection (2)(c)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `use of the statement is sought by virtue of subsection (2)(c)`)
            THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A statement may not be used by virtue of subsection (2)(c) unless— (a) evidence relating to it is adduced, or (b) a question relating to it is asked"
        IF `evidence relating to it is adduced by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution` OR `a question relating to it is asked by or on behalf of the person in the proceedings arising out of the prosecution`
            THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:517 | (4) In subsection (2)(b) the reference to a prosecution for perjury is—
-- src:518 | (a) in the case of England and Wales, a reference to a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911;
-- src:519 | (b) in the case of Northern Ireland, a reference to a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (S.I. 1979/1714 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 22C(4) (src:517-519)
GIVEN `in England and Wales, it is a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in Northern Ireland, it is a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22C(4) the prosecution is a prosecution for perjury` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `in England and Wales, it is a prosecution for an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911` OR `in Northern Ireland, it is a prosecution for an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names the offence for England and Wales and for Northern Ireland and nothing for Scotland
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 22D Appeals`

-- src:521 | (1) An appeal from a decision on an application for an information order lies to the relevant appeal court.
@ref s 22D(1) (src:521)
GIVEN `the decision is a decision on an application for an information order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22D(1) an appeal lies to the relevant appeal court` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the decision is a decision on an application for an information order` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal from a decision on an application for an information order lies to the relevant appeal court." (a decision on anything else is outside the subsection)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:522 | (2) An appeal under this section lies at the instance of any person who was a party to the proceedings on the application.
@ref s 22D(2) (src:522)
GIVEN `the person was a party to the proceedings on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22D(2) the person may bring the appeal` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person was a party to the proceedings on the application` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal under this section lies at the instance of any person who was a party to the proceedings on the application." (a person who was not a party is not said to lack a right of appeal)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:523 | (3) The “relevant appeal court” is—
-- src:524 | (a) the Crown Court, in the case of a decision made by a magistrates’ court in England and Wales;
-- src:525 | (b) a county court, in the case of a decision made by a magistrates’ court in Northern Ireland;
-- src:526 | (c) the Sheriff Appeal Court, in the case of a decision made by the sheriff.
@ref s 22D(3) (src:523-526)
GIVEN `the court that made the decision` IS A `Court that decided`
GIVETH AN `Appeal court`
DECIDE `s 22D(3) the relevant appeal court` IS
    CONSIDER `the court that made the decision`
    WHEN `a magistrates court in England and Wales` THEN `the Crown Court`
    WHEN `a magistrates court in Northern Ireland` THEN `a county court`
    WHEN `the sheriff` THEN `the Sheriff Appeal Court`

-- src:527 | (4) On an appeal under this section the relevant appeal court may—
-- src:528 | (a) make or (as the case may be) discharge an information order, or
-- src:529 | (b) vary the order.
@ref s 22D(4) (src:527-529)
GIVEN `the appeal is an appeal under s 22D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22D(4) the relevant appeal court may make, discharge or vary the order` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appeal is an appeal under s 22D` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an appeal under this section the relevant appeal court may— (a) make or (as the case may be) discharge an information order, or (b) vary the order." (the power is given for an appeal under this section only)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 22E Supplementary`

-- src:531 | (1) An information order does not confer the right to require a person to provide privileged information.
@ref s 22E(1) (src:531)
GIVEN `the information is privileged information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22E(1) the information order confers the right to require the information` IS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An information order does not confer the right to require a person to provide privileged information."
        IF `the information is privileged information` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not confer the right to require a person to provide privileged information" (for other information the subsection says nothing; the right comes from s 22B(3))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:532 | (2) “Privileged information” is information which a person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court or, in Scotland, legal privilege as defined by section 412 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.
@ref s 22E(2) (src:532)
GIVEN `the person would be entitled to refuse to provide it on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in Scotland, it is legal privilege as defined by section 412 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22E(2) the information is privileged information` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person would be entitled to refuse to provide it on grounds of legal professional privilege in proceedings in the High Court` OR `in Scotland, it is legal privilege as defined by section 412 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Privileged information” is information which a person would be entitled to refuse to provide on grounds of legal professional privilege"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:533 | (3) Information provided in pursuance of an information order is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information (however imposed).
@ref s 22E(3) (src:533)
GIVEN `the information is provided in pursuance of an information order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22E(3) the provision of the information does not breach any restriction on disclosure` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the information is provided in pursuance of an information order` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information provided in pursuance of an information order is not to be taken to breach any restriction on the disclosure of information (however imposed)." (information provided otherwise is outside it)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:534 | (4) An application for an information order may be heard and determined in private.
@ref s 22E(4) (src:534)
GIVEN `the proceedings are on an application for an information order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22E(4) the application may be heard and determined in private` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are on an application for an information order` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application for an information order may be heard and determined in private." (a permission only)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 22F Code of practice about certain information orders`

-- src:548 | (7) A failure by a person to comply with a provision of the code does not of itself make the person liable to criminal or civil proceedings.
@ref s 22F(7) (src:548)
GIVEN `a person fails to comply with a provision of the code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22F(7) the failure of itself makes the person liable to criminal or civil proceedings` IS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A failure by a person to comply with a provision of the code does not of itself make the person liable to criminal or civil proceedings."
        IF `a person fails to comply with a provision of the code` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A failure by a person to comply with a provision of the code" (nothing is said where there is no failure)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:549 | (8) The code is admissible in evidence in criminal or civil proceedings and is to be taken into account by a court or tribunal in any case in which it appears to the court or tribunal to be relevant.
@ref s 22F(8) (src:549)
GIVEN `the proceedings are criminal or civil proceedings, or a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the code appears to the court or tribunal to be relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22F(8) the code is admissible and is to be taken into account` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the proceedings are criminal or civil proceedings, or a tribunal` AND `the code appears to the court or tribunal to be relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The code is admissible in evidence in criminal or civil proceedings and is to be taken into account by a court or tribunal in any case in which it appears to the court or tribunal to be relevant." (the subsection does not say the code is inadmissible elsewhere)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:551 | (10) In this section “authorised NCA officer” has the meaning given in section 22B(14).
@ref s 22F(10) (src:551)
GIVEN `the term is used in s 22F` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22F(10) the term has the meaning given in s 22B(14)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the term is used in s 22F` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section “authorised NCA officer” has the meaning given in section 22B(14)." (terms elsewhere are not touched)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
